  "findings": [
    "exp186 passes hard-cut SSIM in all measured runs, while no-floor exp183/184 miss in 2 of 5. With the floor, PVE source-age excess straddles 400ms (see runs): the two gates still conflict by tens of milliseconds at a 10:1 step.",
    "The conflict is one picture: a refresh IDR is ~44KB with the floor against 21-28KB without, ~240ms against ~130ms of pacing at the reduced target.",
    "Native FPS now passes in all exp186 runs (it fell to 42.86 on exp183) because a target above capacity no longer persists for ~16s.",
    "Every remaining native failure is one event: the first ~0.8s after the 10:1 step. Native TCP RTT ~85ms plus 15ms netem. Each ms of detection adds ~2-3ms of queue at this step, so peak packet queue is ~450ms before any reduction; the path alone leaves little of the 400ms budget. Not waived: reported as an open decision.",
    "Playwright enables Emulation.setFocusEmulationEnabled in its own CDP session; each session holds its own capturer count, so a second session cannot release it. connect_over_cdp(no_defaults=True) on the default context gives genuine focus/visibility. First real hidden-tab proof.",
    "\"Target page, context or browser has been closed\" in earlier Mac reports was a harness artifact (finally runs after async_playwright exits), not evidence of a browser failure."
  ],
  "open_defects": [
    "full_rate_recovered failed in exp186 first (4160 at window end) and similar runs: existing high_confirmed path cuts 8000 to ~2700 on a TCP repair under 0.3% loss at 20M; recovery then takes ~12s. Not caused by these changes (also present in exp181/183 traces), but a real quality drop.",
    "Mac harness: Settings click \"waiting for element to be visible, enabled and stable\" timed out in 1 of 5 no-emulation runs (exp187); stale tabs caused another (fixed by closing them). r2/r3 startup failure of 2026-10-29 did not reproduce; its cause remains unproven."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Launch/ACL mocked; dedicated guests only. Mac runs are 40s healthy pilots, not transition/fidelity/long-session. Physical Mac model and hardware decoding remain unproven.",
    "PVE and native lanes sometimes ran concurrently on the shared controller; other agents also loaded it.",
    "Offline estimator replays show decisions on recorded prefixes, not counterfactual live outcomes. Small run counts: excess spread is about +-60ms, so differences below that between variants are not established."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "QSV/VAAPI hard-cut fidelity; HEVC and full VM+LXC encoder matrix",
    "Mac impaired and Firefox/macOS, A/V",
    "Toolkit/occlusion/fallback/lifecycle coverage",
    "Long sessions",
    "Matched RDP impaired/fidelity/soak comparison",
